{"author":{"id":"337a442880d7106d509ff84f2f7fef51acce8bce88b081d4f4c3f0298b7e7941"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791660174,"nonce":"le+c6lzgmufSqwVxY3fu0HOSxDc=","title":"Containers: Containerfile and .containerignore","message":"Spec 018 section Image (ticket C3). Multi-stage Containerfile: builder copies uv from a digest-pinned ghcr.io/astral-sh/uv image and runs uv sync --locked --no-dev --no-editable; runtime is digest-pinned docker.io/library/python 3.13 slim, user jobhunter uid 1000 gid 1000, ENV JOBHUNTER_CONTAINER=1, EXPOSE 8808, ENTRYPOINT jobhunter, default CMD console --host 0.0.0.0, OCI labels. Build target browser adds the browser extra and playwright install --with-deps chromium. .containerignore excludes .git, .env*, data, profile, resume, config.toml, *.migrated-*, .venv, tests, specs, .claude and caches. Add tests/test_containerfile.py that parses the files: every FROM has @sha256, final USER is non-root, no ENV or ARG name containing KEY, TOKEN or SECRET, .containerignore covers every gitignored personal path. Checks without podman: that test, ruff, pytest, hadolint only if already installed. Needs host or CI: image build, size within the budget in spec 018, smoke test (C8); on the host podman build -t localhost/jobhunter:dev . must succeed.","files":null}]}